# Codex Agent — Essora Web SDK: Build Browser-Native Clicky Companion

## Context
We are building a Web SDK called Essora that brings the Clicky macOS companion 
experience into the browser — for guiding users through complex SaaS apps.

Clicky (https://github.com/farzaa/clicky) is the reference implementation:
- Push-to-talk voice input
- Real-time screen capture + Claude vision
- AI response with [POINT:x,y:label] coordinate tags
- Blue cursor flies to the exact UI element via bezier animation
- ElevenLabs speaks the reply aloud
- 10-turn conversation memory
- Cloudflare Worker proxy protecting all API keys

Our SDK already has the backend skeleton. The gap is the EXPERIENCE LAYER —
the part the user actually sees and feels. That is what you are building.

Read the full gap report below before writing a single line of code.
Read our codebase first. Understand every existing file before touching anything.

