### TASK 3 — Semantic UI graph
**Goal:** Give the AI a rich, structured description of every interactive 
element on the page so it can choose the right target without hardcoded selectors

Build:
1. Create src/context/SemanticGraph.ts
2. SemanticGraph.build() walks the DOM and returns a JSON array of nodes.
   Each node must include:
   - stableId: string (deterministic — role+name+region, no random)
   - role: string (from aria-role or inferred from tag)
   - name: string (aria-label > aria-labelledby > visible text > placeholder)
   - state: { disabled, hidden, checked, expanded, selected, required }
   - region: string (nearest landmark or section heading text)
   - formGroup: string | null (nearest form label or fieldset legend)
   - bounds: { x, y, width, height, visible: boolean }
   - tagName: string
   - interactable: boolean (can receive click/focus)
3. Filter out: hidden elements, elements with opacity 0, 
   elements outside viewport by more than 2 viewport heights,
   elements matched by Redaction.ts rules.
4. Max 120 nodes per snapshot. If more: keep all interactable elements 
   first, then trim non-interactable by distance from viewport center.
5. MutationObserver watch: rebuild graph on DOM mutations, debounced 300ms.
6. Expose as ContextCollector plugin — ContextCollector.ts should call 
   SemanticGraph.build() and include output in context sent to AI.

Files: create src/context/SemanticGraph.ts, 
       modify src/context/ContextCollector.ts,
       modify src/context/ElementRegistry.ts (use stableId as key)

Acceptance criteria:
- Graph includes all buttons, inputs, links, selects visible on page
- stableId is identical across two calls when DOM has not changed
- Redacted fields (password, data-clicky-ignore) are not in graph
- Graph rebuilds within 400ms of a route change

