## Code conventions — follow these strictly

- TypeScript strict mode. No any unless absolutely unavoidable.
- All async operations: async/await. No raw Promise chains.
- All animation: requestAnimationFrame. No setInterval for visual updates.
- No hardcoded selectors anywhere. All element targeting goes through 
  ElementRegistry + SemanticGraph stableId.
- Shadow DOM: all overlay UI must live inside Shadow DOM root. 
  Do not pollute host page styles.
- No console.log in production paths. Use the existing telemetry/diagnostics 
  system for events.
- Comments explain WHY, not WHAT.
- After every task: run existing tests. Fix regressions before next task.
- Do not rename existing public API methods on ClickyClient without 
  adding a deprecated alias.
- Do not touch round-voice-437d Worker code unless a task explicitly 
  requires it.

---

## What success looks like

When all 10 tasks are done, a developer embeds the SDK in any SaaS app,
the user says "help me create an invoice", and:

1. Cursor appears from nowhere
2. AI speaks: "tap new invoice up top"
3. Blue cursor flies in an arc to the New Invoice button
4. Highlight glows around it
5. User clicks it — guide advances automatically
6. AI speaks next step, cursor flies to next target
7. Goal completes, cursor fades out

That is the full Clicky experience, running in the browser.
